00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:28.469
WHO MEASURES GDP?

00:03:28.469 --> 00:03:32.870
The Gross Domestic Product is a concept created
by a Russian-American economist named SIMON

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:34.219
KUZNETS in 1932.

00:03:34.219 --> 00:03:39.859
After World War II it was used as a base for
calculating money transfers for the Marshall

00:03:39.859 --> 00:03:40.859
Plan.

00:03:40.859 --> 00:03:43.329
This is how it became the standard measure...
but hang on...

00:03:43.329 --> 00:03:44.510
What does the GDP actually measure?

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:45.510
Come on, I’m sure you know it!

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:46.510
... Or maybe you don’t!

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:47.510
Don’t worry, you’re not alone.

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:48.510
But never fear!

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:49.510
We are going to tell you right now.

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:50.510
In fact, Erik is going to tell us.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:52.870
GDP is the sum of all the final goods produced
in a country or region during a period of

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:54.249
time: usually, a year.

00:03:54.249 --> 00:03:58.499
This means that, beyond wealth, it measures
economic movement.

00:03:58.499 --> 00:04:05.309
For example, if you have oil fields but you
don’t exploit them... it doesn’t account

00:04:05.309 --> 00:04:06.309
for your GDP.

00:04:06.309 --> 00:04:10.900
Also, if you have a factory that stops production
for a year... the factory doesn’t account

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:12.389
to GDP either.

00:04:12.389 --> 00:04:17.289
But if that factory produces one car, then
the market price for that car would be considered

00:04:17.289 --> 00:04:19.870
for the Gross Domestic Product.

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:25.060
So, in other words... more than money and
assets, the GDP indicates the health of an

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:26.060
economy.

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:28.599
It doesn’t care about what you have but
instead about what you produce.

00:04:28.599 --> 00:04:31.790
And yes, we are always talking about final
goods.

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:36.050
So, for example, let’s say that we have
a restaurant and we are making a salad.

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:41.830
We use lettuce, tomato and onion.

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:46.139
Each of those ingredients costs 1 dollar and
we sell the salad for five dollars.

00:04:46.139 --> 00:04:51.840
Only those 5 dollars are taken to account
for GDP because the salad is the final product

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:53.680
that consumers are going to buy.

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:57.280
Another very important thing we need to know
about GDP is that it only takes into account

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:58.360
new products.

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:02.330
This is why when you buy a pre-owned house,
the transaction doesn’t count.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:06.729
But if you build a brand new dwelling and
you sell it, then the market price for that

00:05:06.729 --> 00:05:08.340
will be taken into account.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:12.470
That said... is GDP the ultimate figure for
economics?

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:13.470
Of course not!

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:16.960
If you want to analyze a country’s economic
wealth, you need to consider many other figures

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:17.960
too.

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:23.340
But, so far it’s one of the best tools that
we have.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:26.990
And again... where does the data come from?

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:32.500
Do they go to all the companies and families
to ask them what they produce?

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:34.110
Of course not!

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:35.110
They take samples!

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:39.419
In most countries, there are laws that force
companies to disclose their numbers to the

00:05:39.419 --> 00:05:40.889
statistics departments.

00:05:40.889 --> 00:05:43.530
With those figures, they do estimations.

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:48.169
Then, other international organizations take
the same numbers and do their own estimations

00:05:48.169 --> 00:05:49.169
as well.

00:05:49.169 --> 00:05:51.349
For example, the CIA has its own fact book.

00:05:51.349 --> 00:05:59.349
The World Bank or the International Monetary
Fund has something similar as well.

00:05:59.349 --> 00:06:00.479
And you might wonder...

00:06:00.479 --> 00:06:04.490
Why do we need so many people measuring the
same thing?

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:07.520
Well... it’s because, throughout history,
we’ve had lots of cases where different

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:08.710
governments were cheating.

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:12.479
And this includes several democracies like
Greece or Argentina.

00:06:12.479 --> 00:06:17.550
But wait a minute because there are many other
ways to make sure GDP is accurately measured!

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:21.389
We can compare the import and export figures
or the tax collection.

00:06:21.389 --> 00:06:24.300
Also, some years ago, satellite pictures started
to be used.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:28.849
It turns out it can be a very accurate system
for measuring a country’s growth.

00:06:28.849 --> 00:06:35.490
And one thing is certain: pictures like this
one are extremely revealing.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:40.370
But OK, this is all theory.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:42.280
Now let’s get into the facts.

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:44.300
What exactly is going on in China?

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:45.300
Are they lying?

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:47.990
Are their figures accurate?

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:53.099
Let’s take a look.

00:06:53.099 --> 00:06:56.439
THE IDEAL POLITICAL SYSTEM

00:06:56.439 --> 00:07:00.280
Imagine a country where only the best educated
citizens can get into politics.

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:04.620
Yes, a political system with no voting and
democracy but where, instead of rewarding

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:08.430
empty promises made by politicians, they reward
talent and results.

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:11.800
I’m sure many of you wouldn’t mind living
in a place like this, right?

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:17.229
So this country has a name, it’s called
the Democratic People’s Republic of China!

00:07:17.229 --> 00:07:19.340
Introducing the so-called CADRE system!

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:21.990
In China, politics is just another professional
career.

00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:26.009
Since they have no elections, the only way
you can start is from the very bottom.

00:07:26.009 --> 00:07:32.250
Then, you can work your way up the ladder.

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:36.199
In this regard, the system is very similar
to working for the Big Four: you start as

00:07:36.199 --> 00:07:38.879
an analyst and climb up until you become a
partner.

00:07:38.879 --> 00:07:44.330
In fact, this political system was created
by DENG XIAOPING, the architect of modern-day

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:45.330
China.

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:47.289
Yes, here in the West, we know Deng Xiaoping
as the man who opened up China’s economy.

00:07:47.289 --> 00:07:51.300
But there, he is also regarded as the man
who brought meritocracy to China.

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:55.290
Prior to him, during the times of MAO ZEDONG,
Chinese politicians were promoted based on

00:07:55.290 --> 00:08:02.240
their compliments to the leader and their
praise of communism as a religion.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:05.870
Nevertheless, things changed in the 1980s.

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:08.919
Politicians started being judged based on
their ability to meet goals.

00:08:08.919 --> 00:08:13.530
Furthermore, in 1978, only 26% of Chinese
leaders had studied at University.

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:16.320
In 1990, that figure jumped to more than 90%.

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:20.060
But, without a doubt, the turning point in
this story is 1998.

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:24.949
That was when the Chinese Communist Party
changed the law that regulated the evaluation

00:08:24.949 --> 00:08:25.949
system.

00:08:25.949 --> 00:08:27.740
After that, China would never be the same.

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:32.479
Since then, leaders have been judged based
on comparative performance indicators . For

00:08:32.479 --> 00:08:36.700
example, if the governor of a province goes
to the Central Committee with much worse results

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:43.200
than his neighbors... he is going to have
problems!

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:47.280
The goals are realistic but so is the punishment
if you don’t meet them.

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:51.300
In 2005, the mayor of the town where the XINGNING
mine is, was demoted.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:52.300
Why?

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:55.410
He didn’t do everything he could to avoid
an accident.

00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:58.890
What’s more, there are many anti-corruption
investigations.

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:04.880
If they catch one of those leaders doing something
fishy... that leader can pay with his own

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:05.880
life.

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:07.260
I know, I know...

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:10.450
Chinese Communism doesn’t sound all that
bad now, right?

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:15.600
Well… hold on a minute because, as we always
say here on VisualPolitik, the devil is in

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:21.100
the details.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:22.550
CHEATING AT SOLITAIRE

00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:23.980
I’m going to ask you again...

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:28.190
Who compiles the numbers in order to calculate
China’s GDP?

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:29.190
What?

00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:30.730
Did you say Beijing?

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:31.730
Nope!

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:34.990
In such a huge country, statistics have to
be done by local governments.

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:38.860
And, of course, the local leaders cannot present
worse figures than what the Central Committee

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:40.120
expects from them.

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:41.800
So what do they do?

00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:43.570
I’m sure you already guessed it.

00:09:43.570 --> 00:09:46.070
They tell them what they want to hear.

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:55.029
This is such a well-known fact that even Beijing
is aware of it!

00:09:55.029 --> 00:09:56.029
And you might wonder...

00:09:56.029 --> 00:09:57.029
But Simon!

00:09:57.029 --> 00:09:59.250
How do you know what Beijing knows or doesn’t
know?

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:03.260
Well... because if we add up all the local
GDPs we get a different number than the official

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:04.980
one provided by China’s government!

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:06.209
Yes, you heard that correctly.

00:10:06.209 --> 00:10:09.720
Year after year, Beijing has been correcting
their local estimations.

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:13.579
In other words... in China, leaders pretend
to tell the truth and the Central Government

00:10:13.579 --> 00:10:14.990
pretends they believe it.

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:16.940
Everyone lies and everyone pretends to be
happy!

00:10:16.940 --> 00:10:18.820
Just look at this chart.

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:22.970
Here you can see the comparison.

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:23.970
The blue line represents the official figure
in each year.

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:24.970
The red line represents the aggregate figure
we would get if we add up all the local GDPs.

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:25.970
Of course, if the numbers were accurate, both
lines would be overlapping.

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:26.970
But, as you can see, they never do.

00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:27.970
In fact, we can see a pattern here.

00:10:27.970 --> 00:10:28.970
Until 2006, local GDP was lower than the official
one.

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:30.300
After that year, it is the other way around.

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:34.920
This could be an unintended consequence of
this meritocracy policy that was coming into

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:36.540
effect by that time.

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:41.510
Now the local leaders are expected to do as
well as possible to get promoted so they inflate

00:10:41.510 --> 00:10:46.130
their figures.

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:48.470
But there is still one more question...

00:10:48.470 --> 00:10:52.310
How does Beijing know the degree to which
they have to adjust those figures?

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:54.790
The truth is... we have no idea.

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:58.620
What we do know is how the guys from the American
think tank, the Brookings Institution did

00:10:58.620 --> 00:10:59.620
it.

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:03.110
For example, one of the ways they did it was
by comparing those official numbers with tax

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:04.110
collection.

00:11:04.110 --> 00:11:08.170
It is harder to cheat on tax collection because
this is not an estimation but actual money

00:11:08.170 --> 00:11:09.970
coming into the Government’s pocket.

00:11:09.970 --> 00:11:13.800
And we can always track back to where each
of the money streams come from: this is from

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:18.760
the VAT, this is from this special tax on
this particular industry... and so on.

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:20.579
After that, we can see if both numbers match.

00:11:20.579 --> 00:11:24.801
If China says that their industrial output
has grown by 10%, then the tax collection

00:11:24.801 --> 00:11:26.839
for industries should grow accordingly.

00:11:26.839 --> 00:11:29.560
And, of course, the tax figures don’t show
that.

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:34.360
On this chart you can see, by industry, the
deviation between tax collections and official

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:38.700
data.

00:11:38.700 --> 00:11:42.430
If you look closely, you will realize that
the deviation between both numbers is completely

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:43.430
random.

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:47.250
So it is easy to believe that China might
be playing with their own numbers out of sheer

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:48.250
convenience.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:51.810
And now, let’s hear the final conclusion
of the study.

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:55.350
This is going to blow your mind.

00:11:55.350 --> 00:12:02.360
Our best estimate is that the true growth
rate of GDP is probably overstated by almost

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:05.420
2 percentage points from 2008 to 2016.

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:06.779
Two percent...

00:12:06.779 --> 00:12:07.779
Year after year!

00:12:07.779 --> 00:12:11.730
If this were true, it would mean that China’s
GDP is 10% lower than what we’ve been lead

00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:12.730
to believe.

00:12:12.730 --> 00:12:15.820
Again, this does not mean China hasn’t grown
during all this time.

00:12:15.820 --> 00:12:19.220
But chances are this growth is slower than
what we always thought.

00:12:19.220 --> 00:12:21.030
And this opens the door to many other investigations.

00:12:21.030 --> 00:12:24.360
If they have been lying about these figures...
what about the others?

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:28.370
In fact, this is not the first time we’ve
found something dodgy in this country’s

00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:29.370
finances.

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:32.610
In 2008, many Chinese companies committed
fraud when they wanted to enter the American

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:33.610
stock market.

00:12:33.610 --> 00:12:38.029
We’re talking about non-existing factories,
fake accounting books and inflated numbers.

00:12:38.029 --> 00:12:42.519
It took a team of researchers, working like
something out of a spy movie to unmask those

00:12:42.519 --> 00:12:43.519
scams.

00:12:43.519 --> 00:12:45.889
In fact, you can find out more about their
work in a documentary movie called ‘The

00:12:45.889 --> 00:12:46.889
China Hustle’.

00:12:46.889 --> 00:12:49.449
The movie makers are not a sponsor: it is
just a recommendation.If you’re interested,

00:12:49.449 --> 00:12:51.350
I’ll leave the link in the description below.

00:12:51.350 --> 00:12:53.279
So now I leave you with this question...

00:12:53.279 --> 00:12:56.240
Do you really think China has been cheating
on their accounting?

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:59.420
Could they have other frauds we don’t know
about yet?

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:02.269
